      "side": 0,
      "message": "I think we can add the removal back to the stop() case (i.e. BaseServingState -\u003e UnavailableState)\n\nBut for the unwanted() case (i.e. BaseServingState -\u003e InitialState), there are several errors (some internally generated by IpServer like DHCP server failed to start) that cause IpServer to transition in the same way. Since we can\u0027t detect these internal errors in advance, we have to rely on the ControlCallback for these still.\n\nSince these errors don\u0027t result in the IpServer being removed, it seems unlikely that we\u0027d run into the same issue as b/368713124",
